* ''Removal wins at every reader'' (operator, 2026-11-06, approving the house's defaults; from the edge-frontier ruling "a raise shadows its target at once for every reader that sees it"). A reader whose own fleet frontier counts a device set aside refuses that device's outcomes and its certificate alike: the gate's certificate check and the reader's outcome check both refuse it, and a reader whose frontier has not yet counted the set-aside reads against its last verified view (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-offline-root`>>). A refused cap tip reads the tightest cap that ever stood on its line (`braked`). The law rests in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-swarm-slices`>>.

